# Cheatsheet

Every example runs after `import PlainSQL` and `alias PlainSQL.Dialect.Postgres`. A `#=>` line shows the value of the expression above it. The [README](../README.md) gives the rules and the warnings.

## Rendering

### `render/2`

```elixir
query = ~q"SELECT * FROM orders WHERE id = #{7}"

render(query, Postgres)
#=> {"SELECT * FROM orders WHERE id = $1", [7]}
render(query, PlainSQL.Dialect.SQLite)
#=> {"SELECT * FROM orders WHERE id = ?", [7]}
render(query, PlainSQL.Dialect.MySQL)
#=> {"SELECT * FROM orders WHERE id = ?", [7]}
render(query, PlainSQL.Dialect.MSSQL)
#=> {"SELECT * FROM orders WHERE id = @1", [7]}
```

## Fragments
{: .col-2}

### `~q`

```elixir
render(~q"SELECT * FROM orders WHERE status = #{"open"}", Postgres)
#=> {"SELECT * FROM orders WHERE status = $1", ["open"]}

cond_ = ~q"status = #{"open"}"
render(~q"SELECT * FROM orders WHERE #{cond_} AND total > #{10}", Postgres)
#=> {"SELECT * FROM orders WHERE status = $1 AND total > $2", ["open", 10]}
```

### `identifier/1`

```elixir
render(~q"#{identifier("public")}.#{identifier("orders")}", PlainSQL.Dialect.MySQL)
#=> {"`public`.`orders`", []}
```

### `raw/1`

```elixir
render(raw("ORDER BY id"), Postgres)
#=> {"ORDER BY id", []}
render(raw(""), Postgres)
#=> {"", []}
```

### `list/1`

```elixir
render(list([1, 2, 3]), Postgres)
#=> {"($1, $2, $3)", [1, 2, 3]}
```

### `values/1`

```elixir
render(values([[1, "open"], [2, "closed"]]), Postgres)
#=> {"VALUES ($1, $2), ($3, $4)", [1, "open", 2, "closed"]}
```

## Composition
{: .col-2}

### `join/2`

```elixir
render(join([~q"id", nil, ~q"status"], ~q", "), Postgres)
#=> {"id, status", []}
```

### `and_/1`

```elixir
render(and_([~q"status = #{"open"}", nil, ~q"total > #{10}"]), Postgres)
#=> {"(status = $1) AND (total > $2)", ["open", 10]}
render(and_([nil, false]), Postgres)
#=> {"", []}
```

### `or_/1`

```elixir
render(or_([~q"status = #{"open"}", false, ~q"status = #{"held"}"]), Postgres)
#=> {"(status = $1) OR (status = $2)", ["open", "held"]}
```

### `where/1`

```elixir
render(where(~q"id = #{7}"), Postgres)
#=> {"WHERE id = $1", [7]}
render(where(nil), Postgres)
#=> {"", []}
```

### `having/1`

```elixir
render(having(~q"count(*) > #{2}"), Postgres)
#=> {"HAVING count(*) > $1", [2]}
```

### `group_by/1`

```elixir
render(group_by([~q"status", nil]), Postgres)
#=> {"GROUP BY status", []}
```

### `order_by/1`

```elixir
render(order_by([~q"status", false, ~q"total DESC"]), Postgres)
#=> {"ORDER BY status, total DESC", []}
```

### `set/1`

```elixir
render(set([~q"status = #{"open"}", nil]), Postgres)
#=> {"SET status = $1", ["open"]}
```

### `empty?/1`

```elixir
empty?(and_([nil, false]))
#=> true
empty?(~q"id = #{7}")
#=> false
```

## Idioms
{: .col-2}

### Optional filters

```elixir
status = "open"
ids = []

by_id = ids != [] && ~q"id IN #{list(ids)}"
conds = and_([~q"status = #{status}", by_id])
render(~q"SELECT * FROM orders #{where(conds)}", Postgres)
#=> {"SELECT * FROM orders WHERE (status = $1)", ["open"]}
```

### `IN`

```elixir
ids = [1, 2]

render(~q"SELECT * FROM orders WHERE id IN #{list(ids)}", Postgres)
#=> {"SELECT * FROM orders WHERE id IN ($1, $2)", [1, 2]}
```

### Postgres array with `ANY`

```elixir
ids = [1, 2]

render(~q"SELECT * FROM orders WHERE id = ANY(#{ids})", Postgres)
#=> {"SELECT * FROM orders WHERE id = ANY($1)", [[1, 2]]}
```

### `UPDATE`

```elixir
status = "open"
note = nil

assignments = set([~q"status = #{status}", note && ~q"note = #{note}"])
render(~q"UPDATE orders #{assignments} WHERE id = #{7}", Postgres)
#=> {"UPDATE orders SET status = $1 WHERE id = $2", ["open", 7]}
```

### `INSERT`

```elixir
table = "orders"
columns = ["id", "status"]
rows = [[1, "open"], [2, "closed"]]

cols = join(Enum.map(columns, &identifier/1), ~q", ")
render(~q"INSERT INTO #{identifier(table)} (#{cols}) #{values(rows)}", PlainSQL.Dialect.MySQL)
#=> {"INSERT INTO `orders` (`id`, `status`) VALUES (?, ?), (?, ?)", [1, "open", 2, "closed"]}
```

### `DELETE` guard

```elixir
conds = and_([~q"id = #{7}"])

if empty?(conds), do: raise(ArgumentError, "DELETE needs a predicate")
render(~q"DELETE FROM orders #{where(conds)}", Postgres)
#=> {"DELETE FROM orders WHERE (id = $1)", [7]}
```
